# Remark 3.5 of the paper: theta(j) and PUMP on the half-lines of Mazoyer's rule and of delta12.
# theta_H(j) is observed on a finite horizon H (see src/theta.py); PUMP is checked by src/pumping.py.
# A set of more than ten values is omitted ("not constant").

$ python3 src/theta.py results/mazoyer6.txt 2600 699 1
results/mazoyer6.txt, horizon H=2600, depths 1..699:
  theta_H(j) - ceil(3j/2): (not constant; omitted)
  theta_H(j) - 2j:         [1, 2]
  periods:                 [3]

$ python3 src/theta.py results/uniformA_2-12.txt 1400 300 10
results/uniformA_2-12.txt, horizon H=1400, depths 10..300:
  theta_H(j) - ceil(3j/2): [2]
  theta_H(j) - 2j: (not constant; omitted)
  periods:                 [1]

$ python3 src/pumping.py results/uniformA_2-12.txt 650 | tail -1
checked PUMP(n,n') for 4 <= n < n' <= 650: 0 violations
